IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcin-common`
IMPORT `wcin-dates`
IMPORT `wcin-wirc-2013`
IMPORT `wcin-aca-1985`
IMPORT `wcin-seat-family`
IMPORT `wcin-seat`

-- Victorian workers' compensation indexation notice, Gazette S 363 of 30 June 2026 -- worked cases for the seat of the
-- dependants and family of a worker who dies (wcin-seat-family.l4), under both Acts and both columns, and mirror cases
-- asked from the worker's seat (wcin-seat.l4) on the same facts.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the printed rows of ../../registers/source-bundle/GG2026S363.txt (line numbers in the comments), with the
-- arithmetic shown; none was copied from the encoding's output. The families are ILLUSTRATIVE.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Gazette's PDF, not the published
-- Gazette. Victoria Government Gazette, published by IVE Group Limited with the authority of the Government Printer for the
-- State of Victoria. (c) State of Victoria 2026. "This publication is copyright. No part may be reproduced by any process
-- except in accordance with the provisions of the Copyright Act." Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026
-- (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).

§ `fixtures`

`WIRC 2013` MEANS `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013`
`ACA 1985`  MEANS `the Accident Compensation Act 1985`

`a day in August 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 8 2026
`a day in August 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 8 2025
`the last day of June 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2025
`the last day of June 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2026
`the first day of July 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2026
`the first day of July 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2027

`claimed in 2005`         MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2005
`claimed on 5 April 2010` MEANS `the calendar date` 5 4 2010
`claimed in 2020`         MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2020

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`outside the two years` MEANS `not covered` `the day is outside 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027, the two years the notice's columns cover`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`inconsistent` MEANS `not covered` `the facts given are inconsistent`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`no row under that Act` MEANS `not covered` `the notice prints no row for this under the Act named`

GIVEN a IS AN `Answer` `Pension figure`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the provision of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `answered` f THEN JUST (f's `provision`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS AN `Answer` `Pension figure`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the printed amount of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `answered` f THEN JUST (f's `printed amount`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS AN `Answer` `Pension figure`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the equal share of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `answered` f THEN JUST (f's `my equal share`)
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN NOTHING

§ `the lump sum for the death: shares, 2013 Act (lines 415-442)`

-- s 236(1): one dependent partner, no children: $783,000.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 783000
-- Two partners, no children, equal shares: 783,000 / 2 = 391,500.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 2 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 391500
-- s 236(2): three orphan children, equal shares: 783,000 / 3 = 261,000.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 0 3 TRUE EQUALS `answered` 261000
-- No dependent partner, children not orphans: only the s 236(6) maximum is printed.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 0 2 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the notice prints no share of the lump sum for this family, only a maximum: the Act, not deposited, divides it`
-- s 236(3): one partner and one child: the child $78,290; the partner 783,000 - 78,290 = 704,710.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 1 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 78290
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 1 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 704710
-- Two partners and one child: 704,710 / 2 = 352,355 each.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 2 1 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 352355
-- s 236(4): one partner and three children: each child $39,170; partner 783,000 - 3 x 39,170 = 783,000 - 117,510 = 665,490.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 3 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 39170
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 3 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 665490
-- Five children is still s 236(4) under the 2013 Act: partner 783,000 - 5 x 39,170 = 783,000 - 195,850 = 587,150.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 587150
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 39170
-- s 236(5): one partner and six children: partner $587,270; children (783,000 - 587,270) / 6 = 195,730 / 6 = 32,621 2/3.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 6 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 587270
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 6 FALSE EQUALS `answered` (32621 PLUS (2 DIVIDED BY 3))
-- Two partners and ten children: partners 587,270 / 2 = 293,635; children 195,730 / 10 = 19,573.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 2 10 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 293635
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 2 10 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 19573
-- Before column: one partner and one child: child $75,940; partner 759,510 - 75,940 = 683,570.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `a dependent child` 1 1 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 75940
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `a dependent partner` 1 1 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 683570
-- Before column, two partners and ten children: partners 569,650 / 2 = 284,825; children (759,510 - 569,650) / 10 = 189,860 / 10 = 18,986.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `a dependent partner` 2 10 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 284825
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `a dependent child` 2 10 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 18986
-- The period rule at its edges.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `the last day of June 2025` `a dependent partner` 1 0 FALSE EQUALS `outside the two years`
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `the last day of June 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 759510
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `the first day of July 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 783000
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `the first day of July 2027` `a dependent partner` 1 0 FALSE EQUALS `outside the two years`
-- Inconsistent facts: a dependent partner where none is counted; a child where none is counted; half a partner.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 0 2 TRUE EQUALS `inconsistent`
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 0 FALSE EQUALS `inconsistent`
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1.5 0 FALSE EQUALS `inconsistent`

§ `the lump sum for the death: shares, 1985 Act (lines 30-57)`

-- s 92A(4): two partners: 783,000 / 2 = 391,500. s 92A(5): two orphans: 391,500.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 2 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 391500
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 0 2 TRUE EQUALS `answered` 391500
-- s 92A(6): one partner and one child: child $78,290; partner 704,710.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 1 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 704710
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 1 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 78290
-- s 92A(7): one partner and four children: each child $39,170; partner 783,000 - 4 x 39,170 = 783,000 - 156,680 = 626,320.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 4 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 39170
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 4 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 626320
-- s 92A(8): five children is "more than four" under the 1985 Act (finding 6): partner $587,270; children
-- (783,000 - 587,270) / 5 = 195,730 / 5 = 39,146. The 2013 Act gives the same family 587,150 and 39,170.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent partner` 1 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 587270
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` `a dependent child` 1 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 39146
-- Before column, s 92A(7): one partner and two children: partner 759,510 - 2 x 37,990 = 759,510 - 75,980 = 683,530.
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2025` `a dependent partner` 1 2 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 683530
#ASSERT `my share of the death lump sum` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2025` `a dependent child` 1 2 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 37990

§ `the lump sum for the death: maxima and other amounts (2013 Act lines 442-453; 1985 Act lines 58-70)`

#ASSERT `the most the lump sum can be for partners and children` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 783000
#ASSERT `the most the lump sum can be for partners and children` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2025` EQUALS `answered` 759510
#ASSERT `the most the lump sum can be for children with no dependent partner` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 783000
#ASSERT `the most the lump sum can be for children with no dependent partner` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 783000
#ASSERT `the most other dependants can be paid where no partner or child is left` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 783000
#ASSERT `the most other dependants can be paid where no partner or child is left` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 783000
#ASSERT `the most other dependants can be paid under the other dependants row` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 20620
#ASSERT `the most other dependants can be paid under the other dependants row` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` EQUALS `answered` 20000
#ASSERT `the most other dependants can be paid under the other dependants row` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 20620
#ASSERT `the grief or loss compensation for a close family member` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 10310
#ASSERT `the grief or loss compensation for a close family member` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2025` EQUALS `answered` 10000
#ASSERT `the most a non-dependent family member can be reimbursed` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` EQUALS `answered` 46700
#ASSERT `the most a non-dependent family member can be reimbursed` `ACA 1985` `a day in August 2025` EQUALS `answered` 45300
#ASSERT `the most a non-dependent family member can be reimbursed` `ACA 1985` `the first day of July 2027` EQUALS `outside the two years`

§ `weekly pensions: maxima, 2013 Act (lines 455-487)`

-- s 241(2)(a)(ii): a dependent partner, first 13 weeks: $3,000 (before $2,930).
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 FALSE 2 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(2)(a)(ii)"
#ASSERT `the equal share of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 FALSE 2 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `the equal share of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 FALSE 2 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST 2930
-- s 241(3)(a)(ii): two partners "in equal shares": printed $3,000, each 1,500.
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 2 FALSE 0 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(3)(a)(ii)"
#ASSERT `the printed amount of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 2 FALSE 0 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `the equal share of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 2 FALSE 0 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST 1500
-- s 241(2)(b)(i): a dependent partner after the first 13 weeks: $3,000.
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 FALSE 2 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(2)(b)(i)"
-- s 241(3)(b)(i): three partners after the first 13 weeks: 3,000 / 3 = 1,000 each.
#ASSERT `the equal share of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 3 FALSE 0 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- s 241(4)(a)(ii): one orphan child, first 13 weeks: $3,000.
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 0 TRUE 1 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(4)(a)(ii)"
-- s 241(5)(b)(ii): three orphans after the first 13 weeks, still after three years: 3,000 / 3 = 1,000 each.
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 0 TRUE 3 `after the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(5)(b)(ii)"
#ASSERT `the equal share of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 0 TRUE 3 `after the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- s 241(5)(a)(ii): two orphans, first 13 weeks: 3,000 / 2 = 1,500 each. s 241(4)(b)(ii): one orphan after 13 weeks: 3,000 (before 2,930).
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 0 TRUE 2 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(5)(a)(ii)"
#ASSERT `the equal share of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 0 TRUE 2 `during the first 13 weeks`) EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 0 TRUE 1 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(4)(b)(ii)"
#ASSERT `the equal share of` (`the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 0 TRUE 1 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 2930
-- A partner after the end of three years: no row.
#ASSERT `the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 FALSE 0 `after the end of three years` EQUALS `not covered` `the notice prints no weekly pension row for this dependant in this period`
-- A child with a surviving partner: no maximum row, first 13 weeks or after.
#ASSERT `the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 1 FALSE 2 `during the first 13 weeks` EQUALS `not covered` `the notice prints no weekly pension row for this dependant in this period`
#ASSERT `the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 1 FALSE 2 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years` EQUALS `not covered` `the notice prints only an amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation here, not a maximum`
#ASSERT `the most my weekly pension can be` `WIRC 2013` `the first day of July 2027` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 FALSE 0 `during the first 13 weeks` EQUALS `outside the two years`

§ `weekly pensions: calculation amounts, 2013 Act (lines 464-492)`

-- s 241(2)(b)(ii): a partner, two children entitled: $3,000.
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 2 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(2)(b)(ii)"
#ASSERT `the printed amount of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 2 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 3000
-- s 241(2)(b)(iii): a partner, five children entitled: $1,500 (before $1,470).
#ASSERT `the printed amount of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 5 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `the printed amount of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 5 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 1470
-- s 241(3)(b)(ii) and (iii): two partners, three and six children.
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 2 3 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(3)(b)(ii)"
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 2 6 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(3)(b)(iii)"
-- s 241(6)(b): a child, four children entitled: $3,000.
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 1 4 `after the first 13 weeks and before the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(6)(b)"
-- s 241(7)(b): a child, five children entitled: $1,500 from 1 July 2026, but $976 before (finding 2: 976 x 1.0235 is about 999, not 1,500).
#ASSERT `the provision of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 1 5 `after the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST "s 241(7)(b)"
#ASSERT `the printed amount of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 1 5 `after the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `the printed amount of` (`the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2025` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent child` 1 5 `after the end of three years`) EQUALS JUST 976
-- No calculation row during the first 13 weeks, or for a partner after three years.
#ASSERT `the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 2 `during the first 13 weeks` EQUALS `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation for this dependant in this period`
#ASSERT `the amount the notice prints for my pension calculation` `WIRC 2013` `a day in August 2026` `claimed in 2020` `a dependent partner` 1 2 `after the end of three years` EQUALS `not covered` `the notice prints no amount for the Act's weekly pension calculation for this dependant in this period`

